                "r5": {
                  "type": "_accordion-row",
                  "settings": {
                    "heading": "What is red light therapy?",
                    "open_by_default": false,
                    "icon": "none",
                    "width": 20
                  },
                  "blocks": {
                    "text": {
                      "type": "text",
                      "settings": {
                        "text": "<ul><li><strong>Red light (660nm):</strong> the warm red glow you can see. It works near the surface of the skin.</li><li><strong>Near-infrared light (850nm):</strong> invisible to the eye, and it reaches deeper than red light. Each of the 60 LEDs gives off both.</li><li><strong>No UV:</strong> gentle light from LEDs, with none of the ultraviolet rays that cause sunburn. The warmth comes from a separate heat setting you control.</li></ul><p>Researchers have studied these wavelengths for decades under the name <em>photobiomodulation</em>. In plain English, that's the study of how light may assist the body's natural recovery. Spas, gyms and clinics use larger panels. Everden puts it in a wrap you can use at home.</p>",
                        "width": "100%",
                        "max_width": "normal",
                        "alignment": "left",
